cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  functional-standard-atlas: an attenuation-corrected, territory-resolved
  benchmark of variant effect predictors against saturation genome editing
message: >-
  If you use this software or the derived data, please cite both the software
  (this file) and the accompanying paper listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Ningyi
    affiliation: Department of Biological Sciences, National University of Singapore
    email: cliffzhang@u.nus.edu
repository-code: "REPOSITORY_URL_PLACEHOLDER"
abstract: >-
  A frozen functional-standard atlas of 64,178 saturation genome editing
  variants across seven cancer susceptibility genes, with nineteen variant
  effect predictors scored under pinned pipelines, per-stratum measurement
  reliability estimates, and an attenuation-corrected territory map.
keywords:
  - variant effect prediction
  - saturation genome editing
  - multiplexed assays of variant effect
  - benchmarking
  - measurement reliability
  - attenuation correction
  - reproducibility
